# Catalog

Catalog owns discovery and registration metadata: where templates come from, which external tools are advertised, which renderer component implements a command format, and how IDs, paths, precedence, and compatibility requirements are validated. Executable renderer guest code belongs under <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers">renderers</GuideRef>.

## Choose an entry type

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| define local or pinned Git templates and understand override precedence | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/templates">Templates</GuideRef> |
| declare metadata-only tools or register renderer components and command formats | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/extensions">Extensions</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Use schema `1`, namespaced lowercase IDs, and one explicitly selected catalog in automation. Relative template and component paths resolve from the catalog file, not the shell working directory.
